  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "arx-2605.19780v1-k0",
      "type": "key_fact",
      "text": "This result represents the first observation of charmless three-body baryonic decay of a vector charmonium state above the open-charm threshold.",
      "source": "arxiv",
      "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.19780v1",
      "sourceTitle": "Measurement of Born Cross Sections for $e^+e^- \\to K^+Ξ^0\\barΣ^-$ at $\\sqrt{s} = 3.51-4.95$ GeV and Observation of $ψ(37",
      "tier": "TIER_1_ACADEMIC",
      "authorityScore": 95,
      "relevanceScore": 75
    },
    {
      "id": "arx-2607.22507v1-f1",
      "type": "formula",
      "text": "R=σ^{B}(e^+e^-\\to K_S^0\\barΞ^+Σ^-+\\rm{c.c.})/",
      "laTeX": "$$R=σ^{B}(e^+e^-\\to K_S^0\\barΞ^+Σ^-+\\rm{c.c.})/$$",
      "laTeXNormalized": "R=σ^{B}(e^+e^-\\to K_S^0\\barΞ^+Σ^-+\\rm{c.c.})/",
      "source": "arxiv",
      "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.22507v1",
      "sourceTitle": "Measurement of Born Cross Section for $e^+e^-\\to K_S^0\\barΞ^+Σ^-+\\rm{c.c.}$ at $\\sqrt{s} = 3.51-4.95$ GeV",
      "tier": "TIER_1_ACADEMIC",
      "authorityScore": 95,
      "relevanceScore": 75
    },
    {
      "id": "arx-2607.22507v1-k2",
      "type": "key_fact",
      "text": "Using $e^+e^-$ collision data collected with the BESIII detector at the BEPCII collider corresponding to a total integrated luminosity of 44~fb$^{-1}$, we present the first measurement of the Born cross sections for the process $e^+e^-\\to K_S^0\\barΞ^+Σ^-+\\rm{c.c.}$ at 56 center-of-mass energies from 3.510 to 4.951~GeV.",
      "source": "arxiv",
      "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.22507v1",
      "sourceTitle": "Measurement of Born Cross Section for $e^+e^-\\to K_S^0\\barΞ^+Σ^-+\\rm{c.c.}$ at $\\sqrt{s} = 3.51-4.95$ GeV",
      "tier": "TIER_1_ACADEMIC",
      "authorityScore": 95,
      "relevanceScore": 75
    },
    {
      "id": "arx-2607.22507v1-k3",
      "type": "key_fact",
      "text": "Combining this result with the previous measurement of the isospin-symmetric process $e^+e^-\\to K^{-} \\barΞ^{+} Σ^{0} + \\rm{c.c.}$, the ratio of the Born cross sections, $R=σ^{B}(e^+e^-\\to K_S^0\\barΞ^+Σ^-+\\rm{c.c.})/$$σ^{B}(e^+e^-\\to K^-\\barΞ^+Σ^0+\\rm{c.c.})$, is found to be approximately 1.",
      "source": "arxiv",
      "sourceUrl": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.22507v1",
      "sourceTitle": "Measurement of Born Cross Section for $e^+e^-\\to K_S^0\\barΞ^+Σ^-+\\rm{c.c.}$ at $\\sqrt{s} = 3.51-4.95$ GeV",
      "tier": "TIER_1_ACADEMIC",
      "authorityScore": 95,
      "relevanceScore": 75
    },
    {
      "id": "wp-es-14768-d0",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "Por ello, se dice que el carbón, la gasolina, la electricidad, los átomos son fuentes de energía, pues pueden producir algún trabajo o convertirse en otro tipo de energía; para entender esto hay que tener en cuenta el principio universal de la energía según el cual «la energía se transforma».",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trabajo_(f%C3%ADsica)",
      "sourceTitle": "Trabajo (física)",
      "tier": "TIER_3_HIGH_QUALITY_WEB",
      "authorityScore": 75,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "wp-es-14768-d1",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "Ya que por definición el trabajo es una transferencia de energía,​ nunca se debe referir a él como incremento de trabajo, ni se debe simbolizar como «ΔW».",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trabajo_(f%C3%ADsica)",
      "sourceTitle": "Trabajo (física)",
      "tier": "TIER_3_HIGH_QUALITY_WEB",
      "authorityScore": 75,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
