    {
      "id": "wp-en-68204-d0",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "Extremadura ( EK-strə-mə-DURE-ə; Spanish: [e(ɣ)stɾemaˈðuɾa] ; Extremaduran: Estremaúra [ehtːɾemaˈuɾa]; Portuguese: Estremadura;  Fala: Extremaúra) is a landlocked autonomous community of Spain.",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extremadura",
      "sourceTitle": "Extremadura",
      "tier": "TIER_3_HIGH_QUALITY_WEB",
      "authorityScore": 75,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "wp-en-68204-d1",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "Its capital city is Mérida, and its largest city is Badajoz.",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extremadura",
      "sourceTitle": "Extremadura",
      "tier": "TIER_3_HIGH_QUALITY_WEB",
      "authorityScore": 75,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "wp-en-68204-d2",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "Located in the central-western part of the Iberian Peninsula, it is crossed from east to west by the Tagus and Guadiana rivers.",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extremadura",
      "sourceTitle": "Extremadura",
      "tier": "TIER_3_HIGH_QUALITY_WEB",
      "authorityScore": 75,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "wp-en-62409462-d3",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "The first government of José María Aznar was formed on 6 May 1996, following the latter's election as prime minister of Spain by the Congress of Deputies on 4 May and his swearing-in on 5 May, as a result of the People's Party (PP) emerging as the largest parliamentary force at the 1996 Spanish general election.",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_government_of_Jos%C3%A9_Mar%C3%ADa_Aznar",
      "sourceTitle": "First government of José María Aznar",
      "tier": "TIER_3_HIGH_QUALITY_WEB",
      "authorityScore": 75,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "wp-en-62409462-d4",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "It succeeded the fourth González government and was the government of Spain from 6 May 1996 to 28 April 2000, a total of 1,453 days, or 3 years, 11 months and 22 days.",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_government_of_Jos%C3%A9_Mar%C3%ADa_Aznar",
      "sourceTitle": "First government of José María Aznar",
      "tier": "TIER_3_HIGH_QUALITY_WEB",
      "authorityScore": 75,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "wp-en-62409462-d5",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "It was automatically dismissed on 13 March 2000 as a consequence of the 2000 general election, but remained in acting capacity until the next government was sworn in.",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_government_of_Jos%C3%A9_Mar%C3%ADa_Aznar",
      "sourceTitle": "First government of José María Aznar",
      "tier": "TIER_3_HIGH_QUALITY_WEB",
      "authorityScore": 75,
      "relevanceScore": 90
    },
    {
      "id": "wp-en-7583489-d6",
      "type": "definition",
      "text": "Nicaragua is a country in Central America with  constitutional democracy with executive, legislative, judicial, and electoral branches of government.",
      "source": "wikipedia",
      "sourceUrl": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government_of_Nicaragua",
      "sourceTitle": "Government of Nicaragua",
      "tier": "TIER_3_HIGH_QUALITY_WEB",
